Testament patriarch Jacob, also named Israel. Most conceived of this gathering
as a return of the Jewish people to Palestine.<note xml:id="JSPPJ1_d1e3949" type="toe-note" resp="s" pm:link-target-type="text"><ref target="X6807" pm:link-pointer-type="source"><abbr>Adler, “American Policy toward Zion,”
251–259</abbr></ref>; <ref target="X6782" pm:link-pointer-type="source"><abbr>Whalen, “Millenarianism and Millennialism,”
117, 124</abbr></ref>.</note>
<ref pm:link-pointer-type="person" target="per46" n="Joseph Smith Jr.">JS</ref>
taught that many descendants of the other Israelite tribes—now scattered
