<ref pm:link-pointer-type="person" target="per1388" n="Black, Adam">Black</ref>, a local justice of the peace, was involved in the
effort that season to press the Mormons to evacuate the county.<note xml:id="JSPPJ1_d1e58946" type="toe-note" resp="s" pm:link-target-type="text"><ref target="X5570" pm:link-pointer-type="source"><abbr>Adam Black, Statement, 27 July 1838,
Library of Congress Collection, National Archives, Washington DC.
</abbr></ref>.</note> In addition,
<ref pm:link-pointer-type="person" target="per46" n="Smith, Joseph, Jr.">JS</ref> and others with him on this
<date when-iso="1838-08">August 1838</date> expedition had heard a rumor that
Black planned to lead a mob attack on
<ref pm:link-pointer-type="place" target="plc149" n="Adam-ondi-Ahman, Daviess County, Missouri, United States">Adam-ondi-Ahman</ref>
the following day.<note xml:id="JSPPJ1_d1e58965" type="toe-note" resp="s" pm:link-target-type="text"><ref target="XX5177" pm:link-pointer-type="source"><abbr><ref pm:link-pointer-type="relatedDocument" target="x412">JS, Affidavit, Caldwell
